{
  "$schema": "../../node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",

  // TEST-ONLY. Never deployed: no account_id, no routes, no workers.dev
  // subdomain, and no deploy script references it. `workers_dev: false` is the
  // mechanism rather than the convention -- the absence of routes alone would
  // not stop a stray
  // `wrangler deploy --config workers/mock-ai/wrangler.jsonc`.
  //
  // It exists for a sharp reason, sharper than the one workers/mock-browser had
  // before #186 retired it: that mock stood in front of a binding which DID
  // have a local emulator, only an expensive one to start. Workers AI has NO
  // local emulator at all, and wrangler treats an `ai` binding whose
  // `remote` is undefined as remote. So the moment the root wrangler.jsonc
  // gained its `ai` binding, every harness that boots the site tried to open a
  // REAL remote proxy session against the account, and 8 of 14 suites failed
  // with "More than one account available but unable to select one in
  // non-interactive mode" -- this login can see both Ryan Lindsey and
  // Pixelsonly Racing, and a test-only Worker deliberately carries no
  // account_id to disambiguate with.
  //
  // Pinning an account would have been the wrong repair. It fixes the error
  // message and keeps the hazard: `npm test` would then need network and live
  // credentials on a required CI path, and could bill neurons. `bindingOverrides`
  // instead replaces the binding with a plain service binding pointed here,
  // which is local, so no remote session is started at all.
  //
  // Setting `"remote": false` on the root `ai` binding would also have silenced
  // it, in one line and with no new files -- but it would disarm real AI under
  // `wrangler dev` for everyone, which is precisely what the embedding job
  // built on this binding needs. The cost belongs in the test harness, not in
  // the config that local development reads.
  //
  // SINCE #144 IT STANDS IN FRONT OF TWO BINDINGS, not one. `ai_search` carries
  // the same wrangler classification as `ai`, so declaring it on the MCP Worker
  // reproduced this failure exactly: measured 2026-09-17, `npm test` went from
  // 80 files green to 32 failed, and `"remote": false` did not help there
  // either. A second mock Worker would have been byte-identical to this one,
  // and this file already argues that a moving part protecting nothing is what
  // retired workers/mock-browser, so both bindings resolve here.
  //
  // The name is what `bindingOverrides: { AI: "mock-ai", AI_SEARCH: "mock-ai" }`
  // resolves.
  "name": "mock-ai",
  "main": "src/index.ts",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-09-02",
  "compatibility_flags": ["nodejs_compat"],
  "workers_dev": false,
}
